From f7cb7f2ab18e998c042663a9a4fdd6901c6960ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 06:31:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 177/177] urltest: what the review of r20 found

Before a round a group of fallbacks alone takes its first fallback, not a
block further down. The first round of a group that took over counts as a
round when every member has a result already, and a round cut short does
not count. While a block fallback is the choice, rounds come sooner than the
interval (30 s, then twice as long each time, at most the interval; anew
after the group rested): block is never tested and the dials it refuses
reach no member, so the servers came back only at the next periodic round.
A block fallback is taken without a download test. The test confirming that
a member fails does not wait for the slots of the rounds.
---
